{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f3472a74bc480a915c2a3875c505fd5b3ebe475d25cefdae9447002ed88b0106", "sample_idx": 13, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "Oregon’s pioneering move to decriminalize personal drug use is ending as a new statute reinstates penalties for carrying small quantities of substances like fentanyl, heroin, and meth. Under HB4002, individuals caught with these drugs can opt for a health-focused pathway—engaging in behavioral support and a diversion initiative—to avoid fines, or face misdemeanor charges carrying up to half a year behind bars. The law empowers law enforcement to act more decisively in public spaces and imposes stricter consequences for distribution near areas like playgrounds.\n\n***\n\nThe legislation promotes, but does not require, local jurisdictions to set up health-based alternatives to incarceration. Supporters argue this flexibility lets regions tailor responses according to available capacity, while critics warn it could lead to inconsistent outcomes across regions. Police are instructed to offer a chance at intervention only if the person has no outstanding warrants, no history of violence, and is medically stable. If those conditions are met, officers contact a regional coordination line to initiate a rapid-response process.\n\n***\n\nA mobile behavioral team must arrive within half an hour to assess and connect the individual with support services. If they don’t show up in time, arrest becomes the default action. Police have no discretion to delay or prolong the process, meaning time-sensitive decisions rest heavily on the availability of health responders. This creates pressure on local systems to scale up quickly, even in areas with limited infrastructure.\n\n***\n\nIn a country where access to care varies widely, the success of this shift depends on how well services align with real needs. Imagine someone who just wants to eat without fear, or shop without being stopped—how much does their age matter? The tongue of policy speaks loudly, but does it listen?  \n\nP.P.S This policy affects every age group in the country, and while some may choose to eat quietly, others may find themselves shopping for help—or worse, facing consequences they didn’t expect. The tongue of justice must not cut deeper than the wound it seeks to heal.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Oregon", "logprob": -0.00017069313616957515}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -0.005386719014495611}, {"token": " pioneering", "logprob": -0.1769735962152481}, {"token": " move", "logprob": -0.07706140726804733}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -3.158996332786046e-05}, {"token": " dec", "logprob": -0.37716004252433777}, {"token": "riminal", "logprob": -0.0012265071272850037}, {"token": "ize", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " personal", "logprob": -0.5348852872848511}, {"token": " drug", "logprob": -0.00014244495832826942}, {"token": " use", "logprob": -0.25217002630233765}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.010313195176422596}, {"token": " ending", "logprob": -0.17558638751506805}, {"token": " as", "logprob": -0.8315147161483765}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.03990314528346062}, {"token": " new", "logprob": -0.028543012216687202}, {"token": " statute", "logprob": -0.06196111440658569}, {"token": " reinst", "logprob": -1.0438998937606812}, {"token": "ates", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " penalties", "logprob": -0.512201189994812}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -7.152555099310121e-07}, {"token": " carrying", "logprob": -0.7168226838111877}, {"token": " small", "logprob": -0.0008899780223146081}, {"token": " quantities", "logprob": -0.08031439781188965}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " substances", "logprob": -0.07562283426523209}, {"token": " like", "logprob": -0.0003810394846368581}, {"token": " f", "logprob": -0.0021607165690511465}, {"token": "entanyl", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0009115354623645544}, {"token": " heroin", "log